robotest-supervisor for Ubuntu
================================

The service is deliberately installed disabled and is not started by package
installation or upgrade. Before enabling it, stage a tested RoboTest Lab
overlay at /opt/robotest-lab and review /etc/robotest-supervisor/config.json.

The unit will not start unless /opt/robotest-lab/install/setup.bash exists.
systemd owns and may restart only the Go supervisor. The Go process owns its
configured ROS child process groups and their bounded restart policy.

The default service uses ROS_DOMAIN_ID 42, GZ_PARTITION
robotest_supervised, CPUs 0-5, and a headless seeded Phase 2 stack. The unit
enforces CPUAffinity=0-5, and the child wrapper retains taskset as a second
CPU-affinity boundary. Change these conffile values together when they
conflict with another local ROS graph or CPU allocation.

The packaged child environment sets ROBOTEST_RUNTIME_STATE_DIRECTORY to the
same value as state_directory. Its heartbeat_file is exactly
state_directory/robotest-stack.heartbeat, and the wrapper derives
state_directory/lifecycle-startup-result.json from that same directory. The
wrapper accepts the base /var/lib/robotest-supervisor directory or an existing
writable canonical descendant. It rejects path traversal, symbolic-link path
components, and unsafe pre-existing derived files before reading the ROS
overlay. Keep all three config values aligned when creating a run-scoped
configuration.

Administrative commands, after staging and validation, are:

  systemctl enable --now robotest-supervisor.service
  curl --fail http://127.0.0.1:9080/healthz
  curl --fail http://127.0.0.1:9080/readyz

Package removal does not delete /var/lib/robotest-supervisor or
/var/log/robotest-supervisor. Purging removes dpkg-owned configuration but
does not recursively remove administrator or evidence data.
